## 7. Feature Specification

### 7.1 Module 1: Smart Intake (The Front Door)

#### 7.1.1 Adaptive Request Form
**Description:** A single URL/Slack command/Teams button where any employee submits a purchase request. The form adapts in real-time based on what they're buying.

**Behavior:**
- Employee starts typing what they need ("I need a design tool for my team")
- AI classifies the request: category (SaaS), department (Design), estimated range ($200-500/mo)
- Form dynamically shows only relevant fields:
  - For SaaS: tool name, # users, monthly/annual, business justification
  - For services: vendor name, scope, timeline, deliverables
  - For office/supplies: item list, quantity, delivery location
- AI checks existing subscriptions: "Your company already has Figma. Is this request for additional licenses or a different tool?"
- Duplicate detection: "Marketing requested this same tool 2 weeks ago. Want to join their request?"

**Fields (dynamic, not all shown):**
| Field | Type | When Shown | Required |
|---|---|---|---|
| What do you need? | Free text | Always | Yes |
| Category | Auto-detected, editable | Always | Yes |
| Vendor/tool name | Text + autocomplete | Always | No (AI suggests) |
| Estimated cost | Currency | Always | Yes |
| Frequency | One-time / Monthly / Annual | Always | Yes |
| Business justification | Text (AI-assisted) | Over $500 | Yes |
| Number of users | Number | SaaS only | Yes |
| Urgency | Low / Normal / Urgent | Always | Default: Normal |
| Preferred vendor | Dropdown from catalog | When catalog exists | No |
| Attachments | File upload | Always | No |
| Budget code | Auto-detected from dept | Always | Auto-filled |

#### 7.1.2 Slack/Teams Integration
**Description:** Employees can submit requests without leaving their communication tool.

**Commands:**
- `/reqflow buy` - Opens the adaptive form in a modal
- `/reqflow status` - Shows pending requests
- `/reqflow approve [ID]` - Quick approve from Slack

#### 7.1.3 Email Intake
**Description:** Forward any vendor quote, proposal, or invoice to `buy@company.reqflow.com`. AI extracts vendor, amount, terms, and creates a draft request for the sender to confirm.

#### 7.1.4 Browser Extension
**Description:** When browsing a vendor's pricing page, click the Reqflow extension to auto-populate a purchase request with the tool name, pricing tier, and URL.

### 7.2 Module 2: Intelligent Approval Engine

#### 7.2.1 Configurable Approval Workflows
**Description:** Visual workflow builder (no-code) where finance sets up approval chains.

**Default templates:**
- **Simple:** Under $1K: Manager only. $1K-$10K: Manager + Finance. Over $10K: Manager + Finance + CEO.
- **Department-specific:** Engineering purchases route through Engineering Lead then Finance. Marketing through CMO then Finance.
- **Category-specific:** SaaS purchases always include IT/Security review. Professional services always include Legal review.

**Conditions available:**
- Amount thresholds (single or cumulative per period)
- Department
- Category
- Vendor (new vs. existing)
- Budget remaining (% consumed triggers additional approval)
- Requester role/level
- Custom fields

#### 7.2.2 Smart Routing
**Description:** AI optimizes approval routing based on historical patterns.

**Behaviors:**
- If the VP is on vacation, auto-delegate to their backup
- If a request has been pending >24 hours, escalate with a nudge
- If a similar request was recently approved, flag it as "likely approve" with context
- If budget is >90% consumed, add CFO to the chain automatically

#### 7.2.3 Approval Experience
**Description:** Approvers get rich context, not just a "please approve" notification.

**What the approver sees:**
- Request summary with AI-generated context
- Remaining department budget after this purchase
- Similar past purchases and their outcomes
- Requester's purchase history
- One-click approve/reject/ask question
- Approve from email, Slack, Teams, or mobile app

#### 7.2.4 Delegation & Escalation
- Auto-delegation based on calendar (OOO detection)
- Manual delegation ("I'm on leave, Sophie handles approvals")
- Configurable escalation timers (pending > 24h: reminder; > 48h: escalate to backup; > 72h: escalate to finance lead)

### 7.3 Module 3: Budget Command Center

#### 7.3.1 Budget Structure
**Description:** Hierarchical budget management that mirrors org structure.

**Hierarchy:**
```
Company Total Budget
  ├── Department Budgets (Engineering, Marketing, Sales, G&A...)
  │     ├── Category Budgets (SaaS, Services, Hardware, Travel...)
  │     └── Project Budgets (Q1 Launch, Office Move, Rebrand...)
  └── Shared Budgets (cross-department initiatives)
```

**Each budget tracks:**
- Allocated amount
- Committed (approved but not yet invoiced)
- Spent (invoiced and paid)
- Remaining (allocated - committed - spent)
- Forecasted (based on pending requests + historical patterns)
- Burn rate (current pace vs. plan)

#### 7.3.2 Budget Guardrails
**Rules engine:**
- Soft limit: Warning at 80% consumed ("Your Q1 SaaS budget is 82% spent with 6 weeks remaining")
- Hard limit: Block at 100% consumed (request auto-escalates to CFO for exception approval)
- Velocity alert: "Engineering's SaaS spend is 40% ahead of pace this quarter"
- Anomaly detection: "This $8K request is 3x the average for this category in your department"

#### 7.3.3 Real-Time Dashboard
**Views:**
- **CFO view:** Company-wide spend vs. budget, department breakdown, top vendors, trend lines
- **Department view:** Department budget status, pending requests, upcoming renewals, category split
- **Requester view:** "Your requests" status tracker

### 7.4 Module 4: Purchase Execution

#### 7.4.1 Purchase Order Management
**Description:** Automatic PO creation from approved requests.

**Flow:**
1. Request approved
2. Reqflow generates PO with unique number, terms, line items
3. PO sent to vendor via email or vendor portal
4. Vendor acknowledges
5. Goods/services delivered
6. Receipt confirmed by requester
7. Invoice matched (3-way: PO + receipt + invoice)

**PO includes:**
- Auto-generated PO number (configurable format)
- Company billing details
- Vendor details (from vendor database)
- Line items with descriptions, quantities, unit prices
- Payment terms
- Delivery/service dates
- Company T&Cs (configurable template)

#### 7.4.2 Invoice Processing
**Description:** AI-powered invoice capture and matching.

**Intake methods:**
- Email: Forward to `invoices@company.reqflow.com`
- Upload: Drag-and-drop in Reqflow
- Vendor portal: Vendors submit directly
- API: For vendor systems that integrate

**Processing:**
1. AI OCR extracts: vendor, amount, line items, invoice number, dates, payment terms
2. Auto-match to PO (exact match, fuzzy match with tolerance, or no match)
3. Flag discrepancies: "Invoice is $150 more than PO - quantity difference on line 3"
4. Route for approval if needed (threshold-based)
5. Push to accounting system for payment

#### 7.4.3 Vendor Self-Service Portal
**Description:** Vendors get their own lightweight portal.

**Vendor can:**
- Submit invoices
- Check payment status
- Update company information
- Upload compliance documents
- View PO history

### 7.5 Module 5: Vendor & Contract Management

#### 7.5.1 Vendor Database
**Description:** Central registry of all vendors with 360-degree view.

**Per vendor:**
- Company info (name, address, tax ID, contacts)
- Compliance documents (insurance, certifications, W-9/W-8)
- Contract history
- Spend history (total, by year, by department)
- Performance score (delivery, quality, responsiveness)
- Risk assessment (financial health, concentration risk)
- Internal notes and ratings

#### 7.5.2 Vendor Onboarding Workflow
**Flow:**
1. New vendor detected (via request or invoice)
2. Reqflow sends onboarding form to vendor
3. Vendor submits: company info, tax forms, insurance, banking details
4. AI validates documents (checks expiry dates, coverage amounts)
5. Internal approval (IT security review if SaaS vendor)
6. Vendor activated in system

#### 7.5.3 Contract Repository
**Description:** Upload and tag all vendor contracts.

**AI extraction:**
- Start/end dates
- Auto-renewal clauses and notice periods
- Key terms (pricing, SLA, termination rights)
- Obligation tracking ("minimum 50 licenses through 2027")

**Alerts:**
- 90/60/30 days before renewal
- Compliance document expiry
- SLA breach indicators

#### 7.5.4 Preferred Vendor Catalog
**Description:** Finance curates a catalog of pre-approved vendors and products.

**Employee experience:**
- Browse catalog by category: "Cloud Hosting," "Design Tools," "Recruiting Platforms"
- See pre-negotiated pricing and terms
- One-click request for catalog items (simplified approval since vendor is pre-approved)
- "Recommended" badges for preferred vendors

### 7.6 Module 6: Compliance & Audit

#### 7.6.1 Automatic Audit Trail
**Everything logged:**
- Request submitted: who, when, what, why
- Each approval: who, when, decision, comments
- PO issued: details, vendor acknowledgment
- Invoice received: source, matched amounts
- Payment made: method, date, reference
- Any modifications: what changed, who changed it, when

#### 7.6.2 Policy Engine
**Configurable rules:**
- "All SaaS vendors must complete security questionnaire"
- "Purchases over $5K require 2 competitive quotes"
- "No single vendor can exceed 15% of total indirect spend"
- "All service contracts must include termination for convenience clause"
- "International vendors require additional compliance review"

**Enforcement:**
- Soft block: Warning message, can proceed with justification
- Hard block: Cannot proceed without exception approval
- Auto-route: Automatically adds reviewers based on triggered rules

#### 7.6.3 Reporting & Export
**Pre-built reports:**
- Spend by vendor/category/department/period
- Budget vs. actual variance
- Approval cycle time analytics
- Policy compliance rate
- Vendor concentration analysis
- Open POs and accruals

**Export formats:** CSV, Excel, PDF
**Scheduled delivery:** Email reports weekly/monthly to stakeholders
**API access:** For custom BI tools

### 7.7 Module 7: AI Copilot (Cross-Cutting)

#### 7.7.1 Request Assistant
- Auto-categorizes requests
- Suggests similar existing subscriptions to prevent duplicates
- Drafts business justification based on request context
- Estimates total cost of ownership (not just sticker price)

#### 7.7.2 Approval Assistant
