## 10. Technical Architecture

### 10.1 Stack

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend | React + Next.js | SSR for speed, React ecosystem for components |
| Mobile | React Native | Code sharing with web, native push notifications |
| API | Node.js + GraphQL | Flexible queries, real-time subscriptions |
| Database | PostgreSQL + Redis | Relational for transactions, Redis for caching/sessions |
| Search | Elasticsearch | Full-text search across requests, vendors, contracts |
| AI/ML | OpenAI API + custom models | OCR, classification, NLP, anomaly detection |
| File Storage | S3 (EU region) | Contracts, invoices, compliance docs |
| Auth | Auth0 | SSO, MFA, SAML for enterprise |
| Hosting | AWS EU (Paris) | GDPR compliance, low latency for EU customers |
| CI/CD | GitHub Actions | Standard, well-supported |
| Monitoring | Datadog | APM, logs, alerting |

### 10.2 Architecture Principles

1. **Multi-tenant with data isolation** - each customer's data in isolated schemas
2. **API-first** - every feature accessible via API for integrations
3. **Event-driven** - approval workflows, notifications, and integrations powered by event bus
4. **Offline-capable** - mobile app works offline for approvals, syncs when connected
5. **EU-first hosting** - all data stored in EU by default (GDPR native)

### 10.3 Security

- SOC 2 Type 2 certification (target: Month 12)
- GDPR compliant by design
- Data encryption at rest (AES-256) and in transit (TLS 1.3)
- SSO via SAML 2.0 and OIDC
- Role-based access control (RBAC)
- Audit logging for all actions
- Penetration testing quarterly
- HRIS-linked user provisioning (SCIM)

