## 18. Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Low adoption by requesters** - employees bypass Reqflow | High | Critical | Consumer-grade UX, <2 min request, Slack-native, no training needed. Make it faster than Slack DM-ing the CFO. |
| **Freqens expands into intake/execution** | Medium | High | Move fast. Ship Phase 1 in 4 months. Build switching costs through workflow customization and accounting integrations. |
| **Ramp/Spendesk adds procurement workflows** | Medium | Medium | Differentiate on depth (full intake-to-pay, not just card controls). Integrate with cards rather than compete. |
| **Long sales cycles for finance buyers** | High | Medium | Product-led growth. Free trial. Self-serve onboarding. Show value before requiring a sales call. |
| **AI accuracy issues (OCR, categorization)** | Medium | Medium | Human-in-the-loop for all AI decisions. Confidence scores on all suggestions. Easy correction UX that improves models. |
| **GDPR/data concerns slow enterprise deals** | Low | Medium | EU-only hosting from day 1. SOC 2 by Month 12. GDPR documentation ready at launch. |
| **Integration reliability** | Medium | High | Start with 2 rock-solid integrations (Slack + 1 accounting). Add more only when existing ones are bulletproof. |
| **Feature creep / building too much** | High | High | Phase 1 is ONLY intake + approval + basic budget. No POs, no invoices, no vendor management. Validate the wedge first. |

